              "Data science exams test applied judgment: given a scenario, pick the right technique and justify it. Pure-definition questions are the minority \u2014 scenario questions are the majority.",
              "The exam blueprint is the syllabus: every question maps to a weighted domain. Allocate study hours proportionally to weights \u2014 a 25% domain deserves 25% of your time.",
              "Wrong answers are designed: the 'textbook answer' (technically true, practically wrong), the 'overkill' (correct but disproportionate), and the 'buzzword' (sounds right, means nothing here). Learn the patterns.",
              "Hands-on items are increasing: expect notebook-style tasks, SQL writing, or interpreting model output. Passive reading cannot prepare you \u2014 labs can.",
